{"id":203825022419874,"type":"album","name":"Reggatta de Blanc","artist":"The Police","year":1979,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711108.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-94247050-8844-45a8-a459-9b685e759863/mbid-94247050-8844-45a8-a459-9b685e759863-11479720388.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":11,"country":"JP","yt":"WMl1xKJeuuQ","desc":"Reggatta de Blanc is the second album by The Police, released in 1979. \"Message in a Bottle\", a Sting-penned song about alienation, opens the album. It is followed by the mostly instrumental \"Reggatta de Blanc\", (the title being a pseudo-French translation referring to the album's style of \"white reggae\") one of the few songs written by all members of the Police. The instrumental piece came from the long instrumental break in the live performance of \"Can't Stand Losing You\" and earned the band the 1981 Grammy Award for Best Rock Instrumental Performance. \"It's Alright For You\" is a driving punk-ish .","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-police/reggatta-de-blanc"}},"artist_ref":{"id":79640645910932,"name":"The Police","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/The_Police_%22Reggatta_de_Blanc%22_%281979_A%26M_publicity_photo%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":220327530487024,"type":"genre","name":"New Wave","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1514,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":40522642997662,"type":"genre","name":"Reggae Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":195,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":192783654916590,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Reggae Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":6,"year":null,"note":null,"total":194,"scaruffi":null},{"id":229331613223811,"name":"RY